'''Ashura''' is a [[:Category:Rare Cats|Rare Cat]] that can be unlocked during the [[Castle & Dragon Collaboration Event]] by completing the stage [[Trouble Talking To Girls...]] with a [[Timed Score Reward|Timed Score]] of at least 4,500. It was added in [[Version 4.6 Update|Version 4.6]]. [[True Form]] also added in Version 4.6 marginally improves [[Knockback]] chance.

{{Cat Info
|ID = 251
|rarity = RR
|name1 = Ashura
|name2 = Warrior Ashura
|name3 = Kabuki Ashura
}}

==Evolution==
Evolves into '''Warrior Ashura''' at level 10.

Evolves into '''Kabuki Ashura''' when obtained from [[Road to Ashura Evolution (Easy)|Road to Ashura Evolution]] and is level 20 or above.

==Strategy/Usage==
Ashura is a jack of all trades, master of none when it comes to Knocking back enemies. While it does target every trait, it falls short in the stats department with low range and health. It may be serviceable early on for certain [[:Category:Cyclones|Cyclones]], or stages like [[Merciless Onslaught]], but specialized Cats tend to be much more effective due to higher overall stats. [[Fortune Teller Cat (Rare Cat)|Doctor Cat]] has higher health and range, [[Bean Cats (Special Cat)|Val Val Cat]] has [[Resistant]] and a [[Wave Attack]], [[Ancient Egg: N105 (Rare Cat)|Racquet Cat]] has piercing, and all have a higher chance to Knockback than even Ashura's True Form.

